// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  THORNWALL — a tower-defence mini-game, a Garden panel app written in Petal.
//
//  Exercises: paths (two gated routes that merge, walked by arc length; a
//  mortar that leads its target along the route), many entities (swarms of
//  sixty-odd pests, darts, shells, bolts, sparks), targeting (five priority
//  modes per tower, splash and chain selection) and a fixed-step simulation
//  (spawn queue, slows, armour, economy, twelve scripted waves).
//
//  Everything that moves lives in *cell units* (one board cell = 1.0), so the
//  simulation is independent of the pixel size of the board.
//
//  Designed for a 1200x800 viewport.  See README.md.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ── Palette: a greenhouse at night ───────────────────────────────────────

